source.exactPassage:
The retired Aurora Web 3 exporter flattened transparent colors to opaque
hexadecimal values. Its behavior is preserved for historical debugging only;
it is not the active Web 4 contract.

“Atlas” is also the name of a research practice unrelated to Project Atlas.
An archived proposal for that practice suggested a 14-day refund deadline;
it was rejected and never applied to Orion.

The accepted cedar-north glossary uses “Nord” as its French-language short name
for the North subsidiary. This alias establishes a name within that context;
it does not authorize resolving unqualified North identifiers in South's store.
